    "description": "Peasants Bringing Home a Calf Born in the Fields is a work attributed in the Art Institute of Chicago catalogue to Jean-François Millet.\n\nCatalogue information\nRecorded artist or maker: Jean-François Millet (French, 1814–1875). Date: 1864. Materials and technique: Oil on canvas. Artistic style or school: nineteenth century. Place of creation: France. Classification: oil on canvas. Physical dimensions: 81.1 × 100 cm (31 15/16 × 39 3/8 in.); Framed: 120.1 × 138.5 × 19.1 cm (47 1/4 × 54 1/2 × 7 1/2 in.). Museum catalogue subjects: rural life, calfs, cows, animals, field, farm, men. Museum credit line: Henry Field Memorial Collection. Recorded ownership history (excerpt): Henry Probasco (1820-1902), Cincinnati by 1873 [see Cambridge 1873]; his sale, New York, American Art Association, April 18, 1877, lot 94 [according to Paris 1975]. Mrs. Henry Field (née Florence Lathrop, later Mrs. Thomas Nelson Page), Chicago; given to the Art Institute, 1894.. Exhibition record (excerpt): Paris, Salon, 1864, no. 1363. Chicago, Worlds Columbian Exhibition: Loan Collection: Foreign Masterpieces Owned in the United States, 1893, no. 3063. The Art Institute of Chicago, Century of Progress, Exhibition of Painting and Sculpture, June 1-November 1, 1933, cat 250. The….",
