    "description": "Printed entirely in shades of black and gray, this image is in a fan-shaped format ( ogigata ) with a poem in the surrounding margin.\n\nCatalogue information\nRecorded artist or maker: Utagawa Hiroshige 歌川 広重 Japanese, 1797-1858 Publisher: Kawa-Cho Japanese, Unknown. Date: c. 1835. Materials and technique: Woodblock print; koban. Artistic style or school: Japanese (culture or style). Place of creation: Japan. Classification: woodblock print. Physical dimensions: 24 × 16.8 cm (9 3/8 × 6 1/2 in.). Museum credit line: Clarence Buckingham Collection. Recorded ownership history (excerpt): H. Jackson; sold to Kate Sturges Buckingham (1858–1937), Chicago, Mar. 1928; given to the Art Institute of Chicago, May 11, 1928.. Exhibition record (excerpt): AIC, Gallery 107, Ink on Paper: Japanese Monochromatic Prints, January 17-April 26, 2009..",
